```cpp
void Cache::reload() noexcept {
    entries_ = read_entries(path_);
}
```

read_entries allocates and can throw std::system_error. The caller must learn that reload failed.

Make this C++17 update provide the strong exception guarantee:

```cpp
void Index::reload(const Path& path) {
    entries_.clear();
    load_into(entries_, path);
}
```

load_into can throw halfway through.
